WEBVTT

00:48.810 --> 00:52.140
Send the wounded to the sorcerers! 
Everyone else, fall back!

00:54.400 --> 00:56.510
The main subjugation unit is here!

00:57.190 --> 00:58.580
And <i>he's</i> with them!

01:01.330 --> 01:07.540
The church's secret weapon, a mighty 
veteran of many brushes with death...

01:13.570 --> 01:15.610
The Calamity Crusher.

01:23.110 --> 01:25.730
Shagrua Edith Lugrid.

01:42.470 --> 01:45.830
This labyrinth is still growing.

01:46.150 --> 01:49.080
That mad corpse called the dead to it

01:49.080 --> 01:51.610
until they finally spilled over
 into the outside world.

01:52.940 --> 01:54.670
It's the work of that peerless necromancer,

01:54.950 --> 01:56.660
the Corpse God!

03:13.620 --> 03:14.850
Oh, God.

03:51.220 --> 03:53.080
What mighty sorcery!

03:53.080 --> 03:57.230
Unless we crush him here, 
corpses will consume the world.

03:57.550 --> 03:58.300
Yet...

03:59.980 --> 04:04.840
can even Sir Shagrua, the Calamity Crusher, vanquish such a fiend?

04:05.790 --> 04:06.970
Have no fear.

04:31.020 --> 04:33.330
Sir Shagrua will not fail.

04:33.790 --> 04:38.340
He would never succumb to death.

04:46.850 --> 04:49.370
It's your fault I died.

04:51.050 --> 04:54.650
It's your fault we all died.

04:54.650 --> 04:57.350
Why do you, alone, still live?

05:06.910 --> 05:09.780
Die, like we did.

05:08.370 --> 05:10.990
Die. Suffer.

05:09.780 --> 05:12.040
Squirm. Weep.

05:10.990 --> 05:13.330
Cry. Wail.

05:38.270 --> 05:39.270
I can see

05:39.480 --> 05:42.480
all the souls you've sacrificed!

05:43.150 --> 05:45.190
So, you have the Evil Eye.

05:45.190 --> 05:46.290
The Evil Eye?

05:46.290 --> 05:49.160
He was born with the power to see shades.

05:49.700 --> 05:53.200
He can see the ghosts of every 
bandit and monster he's killed—

05:53.200 --> 05:56.290
maybe even the birds and the bugs.

05:56.630 --> 06:01.150
Most bearers of the Evil Eye flee to the 
bosom of the church for their whole lives

06:01.890 --> 06:07.820
or take joy in toying with those ghosts and 
become necromancers like the Corpse God.

06:27.690 --> 06:33.410
Yet Sir Shagrua still chose to fight 
for us on the field of battle.

06:56.060 --> 06:57.190
So that's...

06:59.430 --> 07:01.230
your true form!

07:02.090 --> 07:04.650
To guard that trifling thing, you...

07:04.650 --> 07:07.650
To me, all lives are but playthings.

07:07.650 --> 07:10.260
Do you think you're a god, 
like the Grim Reaper?!

07:10.260 --> 07:12.260
Gods do not play games.

07:12.590 --> 07:15.730
Not like you and I do, with our Evil Eyes.

07:16.130 --> 07:18.870
Do you not delight

07:19.370 --> 07:24.670
in the resentful wails from the 
souls of those you've killed?

07:27.980 --> 07:29.800
I'm not like you!

07:29.800 --> 07:32.510
You should have died long ago, monster!

07:32.860 --> 07:36.680
As you and I strive, indiscriminately,
 to kill one another,

07:40.250 --> 07:45.190
we play at being the Grim Reaper,
 building our piles of corpses.

07:45.190 --> 07:48.190
But "play" is all it is.

07:48.780 --> 07:50.150
<i>What are these sigils?</i>

07:50.570 --> 07:52.390
<i>I don't recognize this spell!</i>

07:52.830 --> 07:54.240
Let us finish this.

07:55.950 --> 07:58.790
My game with you ends here.

07:58.790 --> 08:00.210
Think again!

08:01.300 --> 08:02.790
As long as you exist,

08:03.350 --> 08:04.770
this land

08:05.270 --> 08:06.770
and its children

08:07.260 --> 08:09.020
have no future!

08:09.020 --> 08:10.090
I'll support you!

08:32.950 --> 08:34.200
Sir Shagrua!

08:44.450 --> 08:47.210
<i>My memory... is hazy.</i>

08:48.170 --> 08:52.760
<i>Oh, that's right. I cast a spell then.</i>

08:53.450 --> 08:55.130
<i>Did it activate?</i>

09:00.750 --> 09:02.930
<i>Where am I?</i>

09:08.470 --> 09:09.850
<i>I can move.</i>

09:11.730 --> 09:14.090
<i>But why do I have these frail arms?</i>

09:19.860 --> 09:22.210
<i>I have difficulty speaking.</i>

09:24.230 --> 09:27.500
<i>Both the walls and floor seem strange.</i>

10:00.670 --> 10:03.350
<i>What </i>is<i> this city?!</i>

10:13.650 --> 10:15.580
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

10:15.580 --> 10:16.800
Wait! Hold on!

10:18.060 --> 10:20.090
Is this for real?!

10:20.980 --> 10:24.900
Have I finally lost it?

10:25.490 --> 10:26.770
Contacts

10:27.910 --> 10:30.900
It's me. Cancel the retrieval.

10:30.900 --> 10:32.770
His body's not in the alley anymore.

10:33.150 --> 10:35.110
I mean, he's still alive.

10:35.110 --> 10:38.400
<i>What do you mean?
 Did the hit fail or something?</i>

10:38.680 --> 10:41.100
No, I confirmed the kill.

10:41.670 --> 10:43.230
Anyway, just stand by.

10:44.660 --> 10:45.950
How the hell

10:46.400 --> 10:49.540
is he walking around like 
normal with a slit throat?

10:50.970 --> 10:52.880
<i>I don't understand it.</i>

10:53.500 --> 10:56.000
<i>I've never seen such architecture.</i>

10:56.260 --> 10:58.130
<i>Nor such writing.</i>

11:00.340 --> 11:06.390
<i>Is that a projection spell? 
But I sense no magic at work.</i>

11:01.550 --> 11:06.390
Ryouma Kannagi

11:01.550 --> 11:06.390
Brand-New Rendezvous

11:07.130 --> 11:10.980
<i>Where in the world am I?</i>

11:09.100 --> 11:11.560
<b>Shinjuku Station</b>

11:09.100 --> 11:11.560
<b>Shinjuku Station</b>

11:14.900 --> 11:16.930
<i>Still, just look at these people.</i>

11:18.270 --> 11:22.090
<i>The children look healthy. 
They smile with delight.</i>

11:23.100 --> 11:26.160
<i>This must be a peaceful land.</i>

11:32.430 --> 11:34.210
<i>What will become of that country?</i>

11:36.270 --> 11:42.650
<i>I don't know if I can ever return, 
but I hope it at least has a future.</i>

11:42.990 --> 11:44.930
Rkphfr zr. Qb lbh unir n zbzrag?

11:46.060 --> 11:49.530
Jr tbg n ercbeg bs n fgenatr-ybbxvat obl.
 Jbhyq lbh zvaq rkcynvaing yourself?

11:52.750 --> 11:55.360
Qb lbh haqrefgnaq jung we're saying?

11:55.810 --> 11:59.790
Are you alone? Jbhyq lbh 
gryy hf where you came from?

11:56.290 --> 11:58.740
<i>What? I don't speak his language.</i>

11:58.740 --> 12:01.570
<i>No, I understand parts of it.</i>

12:02.450 --> 12:06.530
<i>Am I pulling linguistic information 
from this body's brain?</i>

12:06.530 --> 12:09.660
That blood on your shirt's 
not a design, is it?

12:10.940 --> 12:14.040
Are you okay? Can you say your own name?

12:15.190 --> 12:17.060
Y-Yes.

12:17.790 --> 12:20.790
So, this is... "Japanese."

12:21.420 --> 12:25.590
This body's name is... Polka Shinoyama.

12:26.550 --> 12:28.620
Think he's some foreign tourist's kid?

12:28.620 --> 12:29.220
Hey!

12:29.220 --> 12:31.430
You've got a serious neck injury!

12:31.730 --> 12:33.320
It looks like the bleeding has stopped,

12:33.320 --> 12:34.350
but you need immediate medical—

12:40.380 --> 12:43.070
Thank goodness! You're all right.

12:43.070 --> 12:44.550
Who are you?

12:45.490 --> 12:47.200
The cops are a pain, huh?

12:47.430 --> 12:48.820
First off, let's scram!

12:48.820 --> 12:49.830
Huh? Wai—

12:49.830 --> 12:51.790
Hey! Stop right there!

12:53.570 --> 12:54.410
Hm?

12:54.740 --> 12:57.780
Do you think something's up, Iwa-san?

12:55.690 --> 12:56.920
Hold it!

12:58.220 --> 13:03.300
Anything can happen here 
in Shinjuku. Right, Arase?

13:04.690 --> 13:06.010
You've got a point.

13:07.220 --> 13:08.890
Now, let's head back.

13:09.430 --> 13:10.640
Sure.

13:23.150 --> 13:25.280
Looks like we made a clean getaway!

13:25.280 --> 13:28.260
Hey, so, do you remember me?

13:28.260 --> 13:33.290
I'm Misaki Sakimiya. That's Ayimikas 
Ikasim if you read it backwards!

13:33.290 --> 13:36.250
Why would you <i>want</i> to read it backwards?

13:39.230 --> 13:43.170
<i>Memories of this woman are 
coming to me, little by little.</i>

13:45.290 --> 13:47.140
<i>Oh, she's smiling.</i>

13:47.710 --> 13:50.260
<i>She must know this body's owner.</i>

13:56.420 --> 13:58.900
Um... What are you doing?

13:58.900 --> 14:00.550
Giving you a physical.

14:00.550 --> 14:02.230
What's a physical?

14:05.360 --> 14:06.070
Whoa!

14:08.110 --> 14:10.280
Okay, you're warm,

14:10.280 --> 14:11.990
and you've got feet.

14:11.990 --> 14:15.250
Don't worry! You're not a ghost!

14:15.250 --> 14:17.830
You're alive and kicking! Isn't that great?!

14:19.170 --> 14:21.870
Um... Thank you?

14:21.870 --> 14:25.170
Oh, don't thank me!

14:25.420 --> 14:26.660
No, I owe y—

14:26.660 --> 14:30.010
I mean, I'm about to...

14:33.890 --> 14:35.850
kill you again.

14:37.770 --> 14:38.640
Excuse me?

14:38.890 --> 14:43.360
Hey, I jammed this through 
your throat earlier,

14:43.830 --> 14:46.940
so how come you're still alive?

14:48.180 --> 14:49.400
<i>Things couldn't be worse!</i>

14:52.100 --> 14:53.380
<i>This woman...</i>

14:55.350 --> 14:57.490
<i>is this body's killer!</i>

15:01.540 --> 15:03.740
Polka Shinoyama, huh?

15:04.190 --> 15:08.300
Only 16 years old and someone 
paid for a hit on him.

15:08.940 --> 15:12.800
What the hell is Misaki's client thinking?

15:13.630 --> 15:16.470
Well, you'd better stay dead this time.

15:16.770 --> 15:21.270
Otherwise, us retrievers don't get paid.

15:24.510 --> 15:27.510
<i>It's hopeless. Just running 
away takes all my strength.</i>

15:27.910 --> 15:32.360
<i>But what is this land?! 
I can hardly sense the spirits!</i>

15:33.020 --> 15:35.080
<i>There are so few magical
 elements in the air!</i>

15:35.510 --> 15:38.430
<i>And this body has almost 
no magic to speak of!</i>

15:38.790 --> 15:41.780
<i>I can't even cure a fresh wound like this!</i>

15:41.780 --> 15:43.260
<i>What should I do?</i>

15:44.100 --> 15:47.710
<i>I barely understand why this is happening.</i>

15:49.070 --> 15:52.800
<i>Yet if I sustain one fatal 
wound, I'll die for—</i>

15:52.800 --> 15:54.010
Hi there!

15:54.010 --> 15:56.850
Time's up on this game of tag.

16:04.290 --> 16:06.270
Oh, wow!

16:06.270 --> 16:08.780
No one's ever dodged that well before!

16:09.050 --> 16:12.780
I think... I might be a little turned on!

16:21.510 --> 16:24.460
<i>I can react, but this body can't keep up.</i>

16:26.740 --> 16:28.420
<i>This is no laughing matter.</i>

16:28.700 --> 16:33.030
<i>Clues to the world I've longed 
for are right before my eyes!</i>

16:43.630 --> 16:46.770
<i>Back then, I failed to grasp it.</i>

16:48.450 --> 16:49.940
After coming this far...

16:51.320 --> 16:53.150
I can't just let go!

16:58.470 --> 16:59.810
Wow.

17:01.030 --> 17:03.120
Incredible.

17:03.120 --> 17:07.050
I've killed plenty of gangsters and hit men,

17:07.050 --> 17:09.250
but I've never felt intimidated before.

17:10.020 --> 17:12.340
I might fall for you if I'm not careful!

17:30.610 --> 17:31.630
What is this place?

17:31.630 --> 17:35.320
This building's famous in my line of work.

17:38.490 --> 17:43.910
They say the yakuza used it as 
a big-time execution ground.

17:43.910 --> 17:46.890
It's just incredible how 
you can dissolve people!

17:46.890 --> 17:48.630
Isn't science great?!

17:48.630 --> 17:50.370
And guess what!

17:50.370 --> 17:54.460
Rumor has it ghosts and 
gangsters haunt this place,

17:54.460 --> 17:57.180
so people steer clear of it.

17:57.590 --> 18:00.930
The yakuza's one thing, but ghosts? Wow!

18:00.930 --> 18:03.230
Isn't the occult great?!

18:04.850 --> 18:07.670
Yes, I believe you're right.

18:08.570 --> 18:11.150
Even with this body's eyes, 
I can see them clearly.

18:14.580 --> 18:19.490
Perhaps those who used this place were 
too careless with the lives of others.

18:20.310 --> 18:24.490
<i>I see. Since I can still 
see ghosts with this body,</i>

18:25.340 --> 18:27.250
<i>then, as I thought,</i>

18:27.250 --> 18:31.290
<i>the Evil Eye is a power of the 
soul, not the eyes and brain.</i>

18:31.900 --> 18:33.340
What's that you said?

18:33.340 --> 18:36.260
Are you one of those people who 
goes on and on about respecting life?

18:36.550 --> 18:37.840
I suppose.

18:38.140 --> 18:42.030
You ought to treat lives 
with greater care as well.

18:42.030 --> 18:43.510
You said it!

18:43.510 --> 18:48.200
A human life outweighs the Earth! 
Twenty-one grams, right?

18:48.200 --> 18:52.210
So this time, I'll get every last gram.

18:52.540 --> 18:54.660
I'll be ever so careful...

18:58.630 --> 19:00.360
when I kill you!

19:01.060 --> 19:04.650
Don't handle a life so lightly.

19:05.740 --> 19:07.340
All lives...

19:13.950 --> 19:15.800
are <i>my</i> playthings.

19:22.640 --> 19:25.340
Do not waste them.

19:30.350 --> 19:31.310
Huh?

19:32.100 --> 19:33.780
Is something wrong?

19:34.230 --> 19:38.610
No, but I don't feel certain 
that my job is done.

19:38.610 --> 19:40.450
What do you mean?

19:41.010 --> 19:45.200
You've done your title of 
Calamity Crusher proud,

19:45.740 --> 19:47.060
Sir Shagrua.

19:48.580 --> 19:51.780
In that last moment, 
when my sword struck him,

19:51.780 --> 19:55.340
I know his spell took effect.

19:55.770 --> 19:59.110
It seemed reminiscent of teleportation magic.

20:00.090 --> 20:06.150
I could see his soul with my Evil Eye, 
but it vanished all too quickly.

20:07.030 --> 20:12.740
Did I truly succeed in slaying 
that necromancer, the Corpse God?

20:13.150 --> 20:16.930
The church observation unit 
sent a report earlier.

20:16.930 --> 20:22.200
All traces of the Corpse God's soul 
have vanished from this world.

20:22.750 --> 20:26.280
You saved the world, Sir Shagrua.

20:27.210 --> 20:29.700
I certainly hope so.

20:31.750 --> 20:34.590
Ah. The fog has lifted from my mind.

20:35.750 --> 20:37.290
Magic fills me.

20:38.190 --> 20:40.380
At last, I can think clearly.

20:42.410 --> 20:44.050
Misaki-chan, right?

20:44.650 --> 20:50.050
I don't know why you tried to 
kill this body—Polka Shinoyama.

20:50.470 --> 20:53.940
But I do owe you my thanks after all.

20:55.130 --> 20:56.150
Thank you...

20:57.580 --> 21:00.940
for bringing me to a place 
so full of magical power.

21:02.110 --> 21:04.780
Here, I may be able to obtain...

21:06.060 --> 21:07.890
a peaceful life.

21:09.410 --> 21:12.170
You're right. The time 
for playing tag is over.

21:13.220 --> 21:15.040
I'm through with running.

21:15.450 --> 21:23.180
From now on, we'll play at being the 
Grim Reaper—a game of killing.

22:56.370 --> 23:00.400
Now, let us continue,

23:01.940 --> 23:04.100
my charming assassin!

23:06.110 --> 23:08.860
You can't pretend to be asleep forever.

23:31.610 --> 23:34.060
<i>She's... dead?!</i>
